From 7b44a5578ee52d62c2c14d086e3ad167e9440f88 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 15:25:18 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 211/221] feat(area): Edit Shape on an empty shape starts the
 draw flow

A shape component added by hand (Add Component -> Area -> Shape: Polygon /
Shape: Spline) arrives with no points, so Edit Shape opened the point tool over
nothing. It now runs the same draw gesture the Create panel runs, on the entity
the user already has: the entity's position is point 1 (local origin, so the
entity does not move), every click appends the next point picked against terrain
and geometry, double-click or Enter finishes, Esc rolls back to the empty shape
and leaves the tool. A finished draw keeps the tool up as the ordinary point
tool, and the whole draw plus the save-snapshot sync is one undo step.

The gesture itself is shared, not copied: PickDrawPoint, AppendDrawPoint and
DisplayDrawInProgress moved from CShapeCreateTool into AreaShapeTools, and the
create tool now forwards to them, so snapping, the duplicate-point rule and the
rubber band cannot drift apart between the two tools.

IShapeComponentEdit gains one append-only virtual, GetMinPointCount(), default
0. Polygon answers m_closed ? 3 : 2 and Spline answers 2 - the same numbers
their RemovePoint() already enforced - which is how a finished draw with too few
points is refused without the tool asking which kind it is editing. Box and
Sphere keep the default and never enter draw mode: their point set is fixed at
two corners, so GetPointCount() < 2 is never true for them.

